  "worked_solution": "In this case, we have to use the identity\n\n$$\n1+{cot}^{2}\u2061x={csc}^{2}\u2061x\\,\u27f9\\,{cot}^{2}\u2061x={csc}^{2}\u2061x-1.\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{\\pi /6}^{\\pi /4}\\frac{{sin}^{2}\u2061x}{\\operatorname{cos}\u2061x}\\cdot \\frac{{csc}^{4}\u2061x-1}{{csc}^{2}\u2061x+1}\\,\\text{d}x & ={\\int }_{\\pi /6}^{\\pi /4}\\frac{{sin}^{2}\u2061x}{\\operatorname{cos}\u2061x}\\cdot \\frac{({csc}^{2}\u2061x-1)({csc}^{2}\u2061x+1)}{{csc}^{2}\u2061x+1}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{\\pi /6}^{\\pi /4}\\frac{{sin}^{2}\u2061x}{\\operatorname{cos}\u2061x}({csc}^{2}\u2061x-1)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{\\pi /6}^{\\pi /4}\\frac{{sin}^{2}\u2061x}{\\operatorname{cos}\u2061x}\\cdot {cot}^{2}\u2061x\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{\\pi /6}^{\\pi /4}\\frac{{sin}^{2}\u2061x}{\\operatorname{cos}\u2061x}\\cdot \\frac{{cos}^{2}\u2061x}{{sin}^{2}\u2061x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{\\pi /6}^{\\pi /4}\\operatorname{cos}\u2061x\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\operatorname{sin}\u2061x\\,{|}_{\\pi /6}^{\\pi /4} \\\\  & =\\operatorname{sin}\u2061(\\frac{\\pi }{4})-\\operatorname{sin}\u2061(\\frac{\\pi }{6}) \\\\  & =\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}-\\frac{1}{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{\\sqrt{2}-1}{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
